text.section:
A party adopts the terms of a mass-market license for purposes of § 59.1-502.8 only if the party agrees to the license, such as by manifesting assent, before or during the party's initial performance or use of or access to the information. A term is not part of the license if:

the term is unconscionable or is unenforceable under § 59.1-501.5 (a) or (b);


subject to § 59.1-503.1, the term conflicts with a term to which the parties to the license have expressly agreed;


under § 59.1-501.13:1, the licensee does not have an opportunity to review the term before agreeing to it; or


the term is not available for viewing before and after assent:
